'''''Panjiangosteus''''' is an [[Extinction|extinct]] [[Monotypic taxon|monotypic genus]] of [[Antarctaspidae|antarctaspid]] [[Arthrodira|arthrodire]] that lived in what is now China during the [[Pragian]] [[Stage (stratigraphy)|stage]] of the [[Early Devonian]] [[Geologic time scale|period]].

== Description ==
The [[type species]] of the [[genus]], ''Panjiangosteus eurycephala'', possessed a broad [[skull roof]]. Its neck joint was unique among arthrodires and had a ventral laminar ridge and a vertical dermal articular facet; its neck joint bore a resemblance to those of [[Petalichthyidae|petalichthyids]].<ref>{{Cite journal |last1=Xue |first1=Qinyuan |last2=Guan |first2=Qi |last3=Xian |first3=Zumin |last4=Mo |first4=Xiong |last5=Zhao |first5=Yingtian |last6=Li |first6=Qiang |last7=Zhu |first7=Youan |last8=Zhu |first8=Min |date=12 March 2026 |title=A new antarctaspid (Placodermi, Arthrodira) from the Lower Devonian of Yunnan, China |url=https://www.tandfonline.com/doi/full/10.1080/02724634.2026.2621682#d1e428 |journal=[[Journal of Vertebrate Paleontology]] |language=en |doi=10.1080/02724634.2026.2621682 |issn=0272-4634 |access-date=11 April 2026 |via=Taylor and Francis Online|url-access=subscription }}</ref>

